\section{Molecular Proteostasis: Reaction-Diffusion PDE System}

Let $m(\mathbf{x},t)$ denote monomer concentration and $f(\mathbf{x},t)$ denote 
aggregate concentration. Their evolution is governed by:

\begin{align}
\frac{\partial m}{\partial t}
&= D_m \nabla^2 m
- k_{\text{nuc}} m^2
- k_{\text{elong}} m f
- \Gamma_{\text{clear}}(\mathbf{x},t)\, m, \\
\frac{\partial f}{\partial t}
&= D_f \nabla^2 f
+ k_{\text{nuc}} m^2
+ k_{\text{elong}} m f
- \Gamma_{\text{clear}}(\mathbf{x},t)\, f.
\end{align}

Eradication invariant:
\[
\int_{\Omega} \frac{\partial f}{\partial t}\, d\mathbf{x} < 0.
\]

